course: dictionary
lesson: 6355
title: Mown and mown down
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mown is a word about cutting grass. It is the past form of the verb mow, so you will see it after words like «has» or «been»: the grass has been mown. Mowed also means the same thing and is correct too, so you may see both.
explain: Context helps again. «Motorway verges are rarely mown, so they are full of voles.» Verges are the grassy strips beside a road. If they are rarely cut, they grow long, and long grass is where voles hide. So mown must mean cut short.
explain: Mown can also describe grass that has just been cut, as in «newly mown lawn». Newly means recently, so newly mown means freshly cut. Be careful with «mown down», which is an older, literary use. It means killed in large numbers, so read the sentence around it before you decide.
fact: Mow means to cut grass or hay, using a mower or a scythe.
fact: Mown is the past form of mow, and mowed is also correct, so both «has mown» and «has mowed» are right.
fact: «Freshly mown» means cut very recently, like a lawn that was mown this morning.
fact: «Mown down» is a literary phrase meaning killed in large numbers, often in war stories.
fact: Motorway verges are the grassy strips beside a road, and they are rarely mown, so they are full of voles.
exercise: «Motorway verges are rarely mown, so they are full of voles.» What does mown mean here? | Driven over by cars | Washed clean by rain | Painted bright green | *Cut short
exercise: Fill the gap: The lawn was freshly ___ before the party. | mowing | mow | mows | *mown
exercise: In a war story, «the line of soldiers was mown down» means what? | They were lost in the mist | *They were killed in large numbers | They were cut with a scythe in a field | They were painted in camouflage
test: «The smell of freshly mown grass fills the park on a summer day.» What does freshly mean here? | *Recently | Wet | Dull | Old
test: Which word means to cut grass with a mower? | mole | mourn | mound | *mow
exam: In a war story, «the soldiers were mown down», what does mown down mean? | Cut with a scythe in a field | Hidden under leaves | Lost in the mist | *Killed in large numbers
